  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Lingering low level moisture, light winds and \nrecent rainfall have lead to areas of fog and stratus developing \nacross portions of the area this morning. Locally dense fog will\nbe possible along and west of Hwy 17 through sunrise, with \nvsbys and cigs gradually improving mid morning. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Behind the front, temperatures and humidity \nwill finally get knocked down closer to normal for early \nSeptember, with more comfortable conditions lasting into early \nnext week. Still some residual moisture lingering today and \nwill likely see sct showers and iso storms this afternoon and \nearly evening. Best chances across the south and southwest\nforecast area. Then heading into early week, the trend is drier\nas high pressure builds in from the north. Highs in the mid 80s\nwith lows in the 60s is fcst and is where our temps should be \nfor the first half of September.",
